course: dictionary
lesson: 670
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Balance is a good example. «Keep your balance» means staying steady so you do not fall. «A balanced diet» means the right mix of foods.
explain: A balance can also be a scale with two pans. When it balances, both sides weigh the same. In maths, an equation works like a balance: both sides must be equal.
explain: Balance can also mean money. The bank balance is how much money is left in your account. Look at the clues around the word. If the sentence is about falling, food, weighing or money, the context shows you which meaning to use.
explain: «On balance» means after thinking about everything. In «people disagree about whether it balances out», balances out means the good and the bad even each other out. Put your meaning into the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: Balance is a noun and a verb: you can have a balance, or you can balance something.
fact: «Balance» means being steady so you do not fall, as in «keep your balance».
fact: «Balance» can mean a scale with two pans; when both sides weigh the same, it balances.
fact: «A balanced diet» has the right mix of different kinds of food.
fact: «Bank balance» means the money left in an account.
exercise: In «She kept her balance on the narrow beam», what does balance mean? | *Staying steady so she does not fall | A scale with two pans | A healthy mix of food | The money in her bank account
exercise: In «A balanced diet has some of each kind of food», what does balanced mean? | Being empty | Falling over | Weighing exactly one kilo | *Having the right mix of each kind
exercise: In maths, «When the scale balances, both pans weigh the same.» What does balances mean here? | Nobody can see the scale | One side is much heavier | *Both sides are equal in weight | The scale has broken
test: «The bank balance was only ten pounds.» What does balance mean here? | A scale with two pans | A kind of food | Staying steady | *The money left in an account
test: In «On balance, the new robots were helpful», what does on balance mean? | Weighing the robots on a scale | Sorting money into piles | Holding something heavy | *After thinking about everything
exam: In «Cats are agile and good at balancing», what does balancing mean? | Counting their food | Sleeping all day | Weighing themselves on a scale | *Keeping steady on their feet
